1. GRANT OF LICENSE
   1.1 General. Subject to this Agreement and to any order form,
   subscription or license key issued to you, Uptimesoft grants you a
   limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to install
   and use the Software, in object-code form only, and only for the
   number of monitored targets and the term authorized by your license
   key or subscription. Except as Sections 1.2 and 1.3 provide, you may
   install the Software only on systems you own or control and use it
   solely for monitoring and diagnosing database servers for your own
   internal business purposes.

   1.2 Community Edition. The "Community Edition" is the Software running
   free of charge with the community feature set, either with a community
   key or as a Grandfathered Installation. A "community key" is a license
   key that Uptimesoft issues free of charge to a named person. It does
   not expire and is not bound to a machine. A "Grandfathered
   Installation" is an installation that the Software itself records as
   having existed before a community key became required; an
   installation is not grandfathered merely because it has no key. A
   paid license key may provide the same feature set for more database
   servers; Section 1.1 governs that use. Under the Community Edition:
   (a) you may use the Software for personal, educational or business
       purposes, including commercial use, and for Client Services under
       Section 1.3;
   (b) each installation monitors one database server at a time. An
       "installation" is one deployed copy of the Software with its own
       local configuration and data store. A "database server" is one
       database-engine instance with all the databases in it. You may
       replace the server an installation monitors. You may run any
       number of installations, including separate installations for
       several clients, and doing so is not a circumvention of target
       limits under Section 2(e);
   (c) the Software provides the community feature set only. Features
       reserved for paid editions are not included, and nothing in this
       Section 1.2 grants them;
   (d) no fee is due, and no support, maintenance, updates or service
       level are included. Sections 7 and 8 apply in full;
   (e) a community key is for the person it was issued to. Use of a
       community key by anyone else is not covered by this Agreement and
       gives that person no license. Installations that use a community
       key are registered to the key holder's dbexpert.ai account,
       whoever installed them, and report to that account only when the
       online monitor is turned on, as described in Section 5;
   (f) Uptimesoft may, at its sole discretion, revoke a community key
       whose use shows patterns incompatible with the spirit of the
       Community Edition. Uptimesoft may, but need not, contact the key
       holder first, and may, but need not, allow a grace period,
       depending on the severity of what it observes. Uptimesoft may
       also stop issuing new community keys, stop providing updates, and
       change which features future versions of the Community Edition
       include.

   1.3 Client Services. If you provide database services to a client as a
   consultant, contractor or service provider, you may install and use
   the Software, under your own license key, to monitor and diagnose
   database servers that the client owns or operates, on your systems or
   on the client's systems, provided that:
   (a) the client has authorized you to access those servers, to install
       the Software where you install it, and to have the information
       described in Section 5 sent to your dbexpert.ai account;
   (b) you use the Software only to deliver your own services to that
       client. You may not sell, sublicense or transfer the Software or
       your license key to the client, and the client receives no license
       under this Agreement. A client that wants to use the Software
       itself needs its own license key, which for the Community Edition
       is free;
   (c) the limits of your edition and license key apply to that use;
   (d) you are responsible for your use of the Software on the client's
       behalf, including any action you take on the client's systems in
       reliance on its findings and recommendations; and
   (e) you represent that you have given every notice and obtained every
       consent and permission needed for the Software to access the
       client's systems and to send the client's information as
       described in Section 5. As between you and Uptimesoft, you are
       responsible for that information and for your services to the
       client.

   1.4 Your personnel. You may allow your employees, and individual
   contractors working under your direction, to use the Software on your
